<!--
	Unique items: a new item with the same id of an existing one but with its own name, attributes and bonuses.
	name: unique name (shown instead of the item name).
	id: item id the unique is based on (stackable items and containers are not allowed).
	article, description: optional article ("the") and description shown when looking at the item.
	attack, extraattack, defense, extradefense, armor, attackspeed, hitchance, shootrange: optional, replace the values of the original item.
	chance, monsters: optional natural drop. chance is the % (accepts decimals) of the item (id) dropped by a monster
		becoming this unique; monsters is a comma separated list of monster names (empty = any monster).
		Without chance the unique only exists through scripts (doItemSetUnique) or the /unique command.
	<attribute name="..." value="N"/>: bonuses while the item is equipped. Any attribute of rarity_attributes.xml
		except attack, defense and armor (dodge, criticalchance, maxhealthpoints, skillsword, speed, ...).
	An unique can also have a rarity. The definition is copied to the item when it becomes unique.
-->
